#doc (Manual) "Belyi maps" =>

This chapter lists the LMFDB definitions relating to *Belyi maps*, migrated from the LaTeX blueprint. Each definition links back to its LMFDB knowl.

:::definition "belyi.abc" (lean := "TauCeti.PermutationTriple, TauCeti.PermutationTriple.orderTriple")
*abc triple for Belyi maps.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.abc))

The *$`(a,b,c)` triple* for a Belyi map is obtained by taking the orders of the elements in the corresponding {bpref "belyi.permutation_triple"}[transitive permutation triple].

Depends on: {uses "belyi.permutation_triple"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.base_field"
*Base field of a Belyi map.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.base_field))

The *base field* of a {bpref "belyi.galmap"}[Belyi map] $`\phi:X\to\mathbb{P}^1` is the field $`X` and $`\phi` are defined over.
(In the database, we take this base field to be the field of moduli whenever possible.)

Depends on: {uses "belyi.galmap"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.degree"
*Degree of a Belyi map.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.degree))

The *degree* of a {bpref "belyi.galmap"}[Belyi map] $`\phi:X\to\mathbb{P}^1` is the degree of $`\phi` as a finite map of curves.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.galmap"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.galmap"
*Belyi map.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.galmap))

A *Belyi map* over a field $`K` of characteristic zero is a finite morphism $`\phi\colon X\to\mathbb{P}^1` of (smooth, projective, geometrically irreducible) curves over $`K` that is unramified outside $`\{0,1,\infty\}`.
:::

:::definition "belyi.genus"
*Genus of a Belyi map.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.genus))

The *genus* of a {bpref "belyi.galmap"}[Belyi map] $`\phi:X\to\mathbb{P}^1` is the genus of the source $`X`.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.galmap"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.geometry_type" (lean := "TauCeti.GeometryType, TauCeti.GeometryType.ofOrders, TauCeti.IsSphericalSignature, TauCeti.PermutationTriple.geometryType, TauCeti.TriangleGroup")
*Geometry type of a Belyi map.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.geometry_type))

A {bpref "belyi.galmap"}[Belyi map] corresponds to a finite index subgroup of a {bpref "group.triangle_group"}[triangle group] $`\Delta(a,b,c)`. The *geometry type* of a Belyi map is spherical, Euclidean, or hyperbolic according to $`\frac{1}{a}+\frac{1}{b}+\frac{1}{c}` being $`>1`, $`=1`, or $`<1`, respectively.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.galmap"}[] {uses "group.triangle_group"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.group" (lean := "TauCeti.PermutationTriple.IsConnected, TauCeti.PermutationTriple.monodromyGroup, TauCeti.TransitiveGroupLabel")
*Monodromy group of a Belyi map.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.group))

The *monodromy group* of a Belyi map $`\phi \colon X \to \mathbb{P}^1` of {bpref "belyi.degree"}[degree] $`d` is the transitive subgroup of $`S_d` generated by its associated transitive permutation triple $`\sigma`.  This group is the {bpref "curve.highergenus.aut.monodromy"}[geometric monodromy group] of the branched cover $`\phi`, or equivalently it is the geometric Galois group of the corresponding extension of function fields $`K(X) \supseteq K(\phi) \simeq K(\mathbb{P}^1)`.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.degree"}[] {uses "curve.highergenus.aut.monodromy"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.label"
*Belyi map label.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.label))

The *label* of a {bpref "belyi.galmap"}[Belyi map] $`\phi` has the form $`d`T$`G`-$`\lambda_0\_{\lambda_1}\_{\lambda_}\infty`-m encoding the following data.

- $`d`T$`G` is the transitive group label of the {bpref "belyi.group"}[monodromy group] of $`\phi`. Here $`d` is the {bpref "belyi.degree"}[degree] of $`\phi`.

- $`\lambda_i` are partitions of $`d` specifying the {bpref "belyi.ramification_type"}[ramification type] of $`\phi`, each written using '.' as a separator between the parts of the partition.

- m is the Galois orbit label, a non-negative integer written in base 26 using the 26 symbols a, b, ..., z.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.degree"}[] {uses "belyi.galmap"}[] {uses "belyi.group"}[] {uses "belyi.ramification_type"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.num_orbits"
*Number of Galois orbits.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.num_orbits))

A {bpref "belyi.passport"}[passport] decomposes as a disjoint union of $`k` Galois orbits. We denote the number $`k` by *number of Galois orbits*.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.passport"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.orbit_size"
*Orbit size.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.orbit_size))

The *orbit size* is the number of isomorphism classes of {bpref "belyi.galmap"}[Belyi maps] contained in a given Galois orbit.

Depends on: {uses "belyi.galmap"}[]
:::

:::definition "belyi.passport" (lean := "TauCeti.PassportSpec, TauCeti.PassportSpec.HasPassport, TauCeti.PassportSpec.IsAdmissible")
*Passport.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.passport))

A *passport* is the data of a transitive subgroup of the symmetric group $`S_d` along with a triple of conjugacy classes $`(C_0, C_1, C_{\infty})` of $`S_d`, (equivalently, a triple of partitions $`(\lambda_0, \lambda_1, \lambda_{\infty})` of $`d`).
:::

:::definition "belyi.permutation_triple" (lean := "TauCeti.ConnectedTriple, TauCeti.PermutationTriple, TauCeti.PermutationTriple.IsConnected, TauCeti.PermutationTriple.equivOppositeConvention")
*Transitive permutation triple.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.permutation_triple))

A *permutation triple* is a triple of permutations $`\sigma=(\sigma_0,\sigma_1,\sigma_{\infty}) \in S_d^3` such that $`\sigma_{\infty}\sigma_1\sigma_0=1`.  A permutation triple is *transitive* if the subgroup $`\langle \sigma \rangle` is a transitive subgroup of the symmetric group $`S_d`.
:::

:::definition "belyi.ramification_type"
*Ramification type.* ([LMFDB](https://beta.lmfdb.org/knowledge/show/belyi.ramification_type))

The *ramification type* of a Belyi map $`\phi \colon X \to \mathbb{P}^1` is the triple of partitions $`\lambda_0,\lambda_1,\lambda_{\infty}` giving the ramification orders of the preimages of $`0,1,\infty`, respectively.
:::
